I actually encountered a BUG on both offline and sep 2026 versions. 

What happens? If you already had a LAN adapter insterted the OOBE (and yes, I BLAME Microsoft for the bug) the win11 OOBE does not see it, it literally acts as if it has no internet, as dumb as it sounds.

How do we fix it? You unplug the LAN cable from the adapter or the adapter from the usb/usb hub. I use laptops so I also used usb 2 and 3 to LAN adapters from tp link. 

Why does this work? I suspect because were resetting the network interface, forcing the buggy OOBE(win11 installer) to look if they found our LAN card, and if they found it the indicator spins because the pc is getting an IP address, therefore getting connected to internet after a while. 

